      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_103c0abe",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: squirrel_life_crisis; hasOverallIntent: non-toxic_self_deprecating; overall-intent-description: The image shows a squirrel resting on a tree branch with the text 'i have no idea what i'm doing with my life'. The overall intent is self-deprecating humor, using the squirrel as an anthropomorphic stand-in for a person feeling existential confusion. There is no toxicity present; the meme does not target any protected group, nor does it contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propagandistic content. The intent is to create relatable, light-hearted humor by juxtaposing the mundane image of a squirrel with a human existential crisis, inviting viewers to laugh at their own life uncertainties.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_79264468"
      },
